{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing","id":852862,"title":"Pack Merits - crowd sourcing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-25T01:45:53-07:00","id":852862,"title":"Pack Merits - crowd sourcing","content":"You may have noticed in Stew's recent <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-pack-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">developer's blog about <i>The Pack</i></a> that he mentioned 'Some merits that apply to the pack as a whole'.<br /> <br /> Well, finally having some info released about <i>The Pack</i> means that I'm in the mood to write Werewolf again. (Who are we kidding? I'm always in the mood to write werewolves!)<br /> <br /> I know what's in the book (I wrote those parts), and I know the extras I've already written to be released afterwards as either an officially stamped web enhancement, or as unofficial forum content. Either way, more stuff for you.<br /> <br /> What I can't yet do is tell you what is included. What I can do is ask what kinds of things you folks think should be pack merits? Give me your ideas - I'll take the ones that fit the systems in <i>The Pack</i> and aren't already done and write them up alongside the other bonus merits.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately you won't find out which I've done (or how they look) until after <i>The Pack</i> is released, but that shouldn't be too much longer. (He said, hopefully.)<br /> <br /> So whaddya say, forumites? Anyone have any merits they think a pack (as a whole) needs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T02:37:15-07:00","id":852866,"title":"","content":"I'd like things that enhance extended rolls. Not just the teamwork rules, but something like adding additional rolls per additional packmate would be neat.<br /> <br /> Something in the social arena would be lovely. Like switching your own dice rolls with that of a packmate when dealing with a group they're familiar with or something.<br /> <br /> 5:30 am and inebration aren't helping me get my thoughts out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T02:52:05-07:00","id":852868,"title":"","content":"Some ideas from me:<ul><li><b>Pack Tracking</b> - because (most) wolves are not Lone Wolves. Your human packmates can help you find Prey in the city or woods. Probably even bonus to Chases also.</li> <li><b>&quot;These aren't the Uratha you're looking for&quot;</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"> - in numbers are strength. There is also safety. Whole pack can assure to hide more easily it's members in it's midst.</span></span></li> <li><b>We are FAMILY</b> - Pack works as universal Flesh Touchstone to all it's members ( even Totem or spirits ).</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-25-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:04:06-07:00","id":852998,"title":"","content":"I suppose I see most of pack stuff as also territory stuff. So maybe some sort of 'False Trails,' merit that works as a sort of pseudo security, a lesser, mundane form of Maze Ward designed for anyone trying to track down members of the pack, it would increase the time required by a certain amount depending upon the Merit dots. I figure it would either be tied into or there would be a separate Merit that had a chance to warn you if someone was searching or asking around for packmates within the territory. That said I understand there are, for the first at least, gifts that can emulate this, but this would be an entirely mundane thing wolf-blooded and others could help with if one didn't have the necessary facets.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a sort of miniature spirit court merit, something that represents a kind of spirit you have curried favors with and are more likely to lean on your side or look out for you or send you warnings, but only with the minor ranked spirits. I guess that could fit under Contacts or Allies, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-25-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:17:12-07:00","id":853006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=852998#post852998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a sort of miniature spirit court merit, something that represents a kind of spirit you have curried favors with and are more likely to lean on your side or look out for you or send you warnings, but only with the minor ranked spirits. I guess that could fit under Contacts or Allies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was just thinking about something like this as the forum was loading. Perhaps some way for the pack to understand the context of its ecological/political standing within the courts of the spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:23:55-07:00","id":853015,"title":"","content":"Territory features?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:28:02-07:00","id":853018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853006#post853006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was just thinking about something like this as the forum was loading. Perhaps some way for the pack to understand the context of its ecological/political standing within the courts of the spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good one. I want to say Feng Shui but that's not quite right. Something like an all around sense for the mood of things, like a folkloric meteorologist. Noting where the Gauntlet seems to be changing or where spirits are more active than they used to be. Pulse of the Hisil? Noting gathering of forces of one spirit court or another, or when certain spirits have disappeared or 'spirit sensitive' people and locations are different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853015#post853015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Territory features?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to think of something like that too. But outside of Dedicated Locus, what would there be that's worth basing a pack Merit around?<br /> <br /> In one of my first games we had a meat locker. And I keep thinking of a great pit in a place that used to be a silver mine. One of the issues that came up with my first werewolf was that, 'The People Do Not Kill The People,' is hard to have a middle ground with. If you attack someone, you risk breaking it. Beating up a zealot isn't likely to change their minds, even the Fire-Touched have more ways to convert people than simply pummeling them. My character thought very highly of that part of the Oath, which is where the meat locker came in. It was someplace to stash an enemy you couldn't kill, letting them out when the rest of the situation was dealt with. Of course now with the variety of abilities werewolves have that let them get out of places like that you would need some extra oomph. Locating it on a Barren might help. Some sort of 'Barren Box,' perhaps acting like an inverted Safe Place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:36:13-07:00","id":853023,"title":"","content":"It could be cool to see a Merit that lets a werewolf share a &quot;teachable&quot; Merit they possess with pack members. You're good a grappling? Bam, suddenly your packmates are good at grappling too. Or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:56:36-07:00","id":853036,"title":"","content":"How about a Merit that allows a pack to have an atypical Totem? Lodge of Death packs could take Ghost Totems, Bale Hounds could take Magath or Malejin Totems, packs in Tokyo could take Tengu Totems, packs of Su'Ur could take Idigam Totems...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T02:50:19-07:00","id":853409,"title":"","content":"This is a good start. I've taken some good ideas from here - the additional merits have bulked out to about 2000 words.<br /> <br /> Bring on more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:42:03-07:00","id":853501,"title":"","content":"Some kind of pack rite synergy merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:00:02-07:00","id":853517,"title":"","content":"Something I've been considering for my game is letting members of a blessed pack temporarily borrow the Renown rating associated with packmate's Auspice Renown for all purposes (other than Moon Gift access, and probably some other obviously broken things I'm overlooking right now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/704-edge","name":"Edge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar704_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:09:48-07:00","id":853527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853517#post853517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been considering for my game is letting members of a blessed pack temporarily borrow the Renown rating associated with packmate's Auspice Renown for all purposes (other than Moon Gift access, and probably some other obviously broken things I'm overlooking right now).</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a Merit that lets all members of the pack Flare Renown using the highest of that type within the pack? That gets around potential abuses with Gifts and Honorary Rank, and it could be available to any pack, but will have the most benefit for Blessed packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:21:48-07:00","id":853586,"title":"","content":"A Merit to develop a minor spirit court for your totem, offering it another source of Essence and effectively minions who can act remotely. Probably requires the totem to be at a certain rank first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:44:49-07:00","id":853622,"title":"","content":"Maybe a couple Merits granting benefits for different ways packs operate within the human world. Like, a pack that functions like a gang might get certain benefits, while a pack that controls a business (look at the Silver Syndicate from HG:tR as an example) would have different benefits, and one that acts like a spiritual nature-cult would have something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:51:17-07:00","id":853628,"title":"","content":"Sort of like an Advanced Profession merit? An Organization merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:49:47-07:00","id":853657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853628#post853628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of like an Advanced Profession merit? An Organization merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Very much like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:34:33-07:00","id":853681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853586#post853586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Merit to develop a minor spirit court for your totem, offering it another source of Essence and effectively minions who can act remotely. Probably requires the totem to be at a certain rank first.</div> </div> </div> </div>OMG I want this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T16:13:34-07:00","id":853733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853501#post853501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some kind of pack rite synergy merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond generic teamwork-enhancing synergy merits? Can you expand on your thoughts, because I don't understand your meaning beyond rites being a primary actor + teamwork roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T16:36:25-07:00","id":853740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853733#post853733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beyond generic teamwork-enhancing synergy merits? Can you expand on your thoughts, because I don't understand your meaning beyond rites being a primary actor + teamwork roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could have a merit that for instance makes every packmate count a rite-master for the purpose of cost; and Sacred Hunt could grant the tribal specifics of everyone participating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T16:57:29-07:00","id":853747,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:19:44-07:00","id":853753,"title":"","content":"How about some stuff that interacts with the new subsystems in the CofD core? Merits that make the whole pack harder to uncover Clues about, Merits that give the pack advantages in Chases when there are more packmates involved in the Chase, Merits that help the pack Craft plans and Organizations, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:38:02-07:00","id":853848,"title":"","content":"I've wanted an 'organization' system or subsystem for years, I never really thought of it tying into werewolf, outside of cults, until Charlaquin brought it up. So I could see this falling under that but, since that doesn't exist, a pack merit seems like a good way to handle it.<br /> <br /> Some sort of Pack Renown. The idea of personal renown is one that's been around since, I think, Apocalypse, but there doesn't seem to be as much emphasis on the pack. Obviously the upcoming book is about understanding what it's like to be in the pack, but it seems like there should be something to give your pack a name and a stamp in the world beyond the activities of its individuals, otherwise packs are just a flash in the pan that goes forgotten once the last members have found new ones. Maybe offering a collective bonus in terms of social standing depending on how the pack has aligned itself, or their collective sacred hunts or acts of renown. I'm really not sure how it should be developed mechanically. I keep falling back to the '+# to something' but it would be nice to deviate, especially as it focuses more on the results of the hunt than spurring the pack on to hunt more.<br /> <br /> A side effect I have thought about is perhaps the renown creates a sort of reflection in the Shadow. An 'advanced' Safe Place in the form of a Place That Isn't. I'm hoping it isn't stepping on the toes of Lair from Beast, I imagine it being more about the victories and triumphs of the pack, spawned from the knowledge of other werewolves and even mortals who have heard of the pack in one form or another but may not be entirely aware of a pack, like if they've set themselves up as a biker gang or business, the place might form in the Hisil in their territory to look like an imagined biker bar or expansive penthouse office.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:48:32-07:00","id":853855,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, I LOVE the idea of Pack Renown! I had never even considered such a thing, but it's such a perfect fit for Forsaken I feel like I've always wanted it and just didn't know what I was missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:20:24-07:00","id":853874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853855#post853855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, I LOVE the idea of Pack Renown! I had never even considered such a thing, but it's such a perfect fit for Forsaken I feel like I've always wanted it and just didn't know what I was missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! Awesome idea nofather!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:58:07-07:00","id":853896,"title":"","content":"Pack Status. Like <i>Pack Status: Criminals </i>would be appropriate for a pack of gangbangers.<br /> <br /> Also, some kind of pack renown tracker. I suppose that would be an aggregate of the pack's member's renowns, or else simply the highest in each renown among the pack. But I've always wanted some way to represent the influence or reputation of a pack as opposed to the individual members, especially in regards to diplomacy or territory or other pack on pack encounters.<br /> <br /> I also once played a game where the GM had pack archetypes that granted bonuses if one had an accepted role in the pack. There was Alpha, Omega, Scout, Diplomat, Soldier, Advisor, etc. They essentially functioned as Pack-based Anchors, I guess. I don't know, maybe that isn't a thing we need.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mostly what I want, which may or may not be impinging on Pack Tactics, is Pack Fighting Styles.<br /> <br /> Sort of like a way the pack fights. Tiered merits that each member can contribute to but everyone benefits from. Maybe only one dot per member, even.<br /> <br /> Like a pack that likes to gang their enemies and tear them apart one by one might have a bonus to attacking opponents already in a grapple with one of their members. Or treat a grapple as a Hold, and a Hold as Restrained. That might be too much. Or might gain bonus maneuvers. Or their attacks penalize defense by 2 instead of 1 (is that still a thing in 2e? I have been using it, but I just realized I might not have actually seen it in the books).<br /> <br /> Or a pack that fights guerrila warfare style, hit and run, ambush tactics, etc. Might have something that allows them all to attack at once on an ambush. Or a pack that revels in all-out brawls might get a bonus to resolve when outnumbered (equivalent to the difference), or give a penalty to opponent's resolve when they have the numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I guess I was beaten to the pack renown idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:20:34-07:00","id":853917,"title":"","content":"How about something for the Human/Wolf blooded members? Either PC or NPC, the idea being that they all could take part in the pack in some manner. They shouldn't be left out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:32:09-07:00","id":853981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853527#post853527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a Merit that lets all members of the pack Flare Renown using the highest of that type within the pack? That gets around potential abuses with Gifts and Honorary Rank, and it could be available to any pack, but will have the most benefit for Blessed packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is much more balanced than my initial concepts, and more evocative to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/704-edge","name":"Edge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar704_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:40:50-07:00","id":853983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=853917#post853917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about something for the Human/Wolf blooded members? Either PC or NPC, the idea being that they all could take part in the pack in some manner. They shouldn't be left out.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I can guarantee with The Pack is that Wolf Blooded and humans are definitely not left out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:56:50-07:00","id":853990,"title":"","content":"While at work I wondered about a Pack Merit that combines the Renown ratings of everyone present in the Pack to determine Honorary Rank. But I see other people have way better ideas on that front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:00:45-07:00","id":854035,"title":"","content":"Man, when dev on Forsaken 2e started I was running out all manner of crazy ideas; pack character sheets with special territory-linked 'merits', pack primary and secondary renowns to indicate what types of behaviour the pack most values, an entire internal/external werewolf challenge system based on the different Renowns and where picking the wrong type of challenge could really fuck you over (for example, in a pack that most values Wisdom and Cunning, say, it's just not enough for the Rahu to challenge the current leader via a brawl for command - it'd literally make the rest of the pack *respect the Rahu less* rather than let them take over. Instead she'd be better off taking one of the Cunning or Wisdom challenge types, even if it doesn't play to her strengths), a pack XP system, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:59:16-07:00","id":856334,"title":"","content":"So, you sneaky werewolf fans, you now have around 3000 extra words on Pack Merits that you'll get for free at some point.<br /> <br /> Anyone have anything else they need?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:38:33-07:00","id":856372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=856334#post856334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you sneaky werewolf fans, you now have around 3000 extra words on Pack Merits that you'll get for free at some point.<br /> <br /> Anyone have anything else they need?</div> </div> </div> </div> More money for college?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:50:12-07:00","id":856375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/852862-pack-merits-crowd-sourcing?p=856372#post856372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More money for college?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bill Gates just paid off your student loans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T04:02:27-07:00","id":856378,"title":"","content":"Lodges spoiler! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We need those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:13:10-07:00","id":856394,"title":"","content":"*sigh* So, rephrasing, anything else you need in terms of Pack Merits? Or things with which I can actually help?<br /> <br /> Wyrdhamster - lodges spoiler is not one of those things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:40:19-07:00","id":856408,"title":"","content":"But Lodges are super packs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No, just joking. As to Pack Merits - maybe you could sum up what <i>will</i> be in book ( more or less ) and we will look what is <i>not</i> on this list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:48:33-07:00","id":857366,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I can't give that kind of detail, even in an overview (except to say it includes Merits useful to the pack as a whole). What I can say is to look at the suggestions people have made above - some of them were already covered by what's included, many weren't. If there's anything you think would be helpful that isn't covered above, shourt it out.<br /> <br /> Another thing I can say is that due to word count limits, the book includes about 1500 words of Pack Merits. Thanks to this thread, you have an extra 3000 coming your way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:53:13-07:00","id":857371,"title":"","content":"I wrote out a big post in response to your last post but realized halfway through it had really left the territory of pack merits.<br /> <br /> Basically I was suggesting, if it didn't already overlap with the previous request for merits for different totems, then a more expansive totem merit. Basically an option for things you can do beyond get Ten Experiences. If you have a massive pack, similar to the way Lycaon-Ur does, with likely far more than 20 Totem merit dots, how does that affect the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:07:31-07:00","id":857375,"title":"","content":"&lt; only slightly cryptic &gt; I don't think we need a merit for that... &lt; / only slightly cryptic &gt;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:38:20-07:00","id":858163,"title":"","content":"Right. I've sent the first draft (3200 words) off to my pack for critique and comment. I'll keep adding as inspiration (and request) occur, but let the refinement begin!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T06:32:46-07:00","id":858306,"title":"","content":"I'm rather stuck on ideas. Once we get the core idea of what is possible when The Pack releases I'm sure people will have more suggestions. <br /> <br /> Now, how about Anchors and Touchstones? Perhaps being around packmates fulfilling their Blood/Bone Archetypes helps them to solidify their own. I would think seeing your packmate perform a grandiose action that warrants regaining all their willpower would give people around them 1 Willpower as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:50:32-07:00","id":860757,"title":"","content":"I guess I might be entering the territory of Territories, but Merits that deal with the piece of land claimed by the pack would be really nice.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is not the book for crossovers, but since the Pack talks about packs, the inclusion of other creatures should have a least a little bit of room. A Merit to allow other beings to act as Totems? Very powerful Werewolves, Mages, an Apex Beast... Maybe this would sacrifice some of the spiritual power but give the Pack a way to differentiate from others and get some kind of edge when living in a territory owned by another creature?<br /> <br /> Social Merits that enhance the Sway mechanics for Alphas, Betas, and give Omegas some kind of benefit? Intra-Pack Sway deserves some attention, since Pack dynamics should differ from human social interactions.<br /> <br /> I also love the idea of Pack Renown, this would sell me the book by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:08:45-07:00","id":860967,"title":"","content":"Packmerits related to land owned, a locus or an important meeting area would be cool. But it should give the pack some specific bonuses related to the area.<br /> Other things I would love is a Pack merit related to other packs. Kind of like pack respect or pack status. If you're part of a well respected pack with lots of history other pack respect you more, let minor incursions slide etc.<br /> Pack favors. The pack can call in favors with local spirits on their territory (or elsewhere). maybe they know a group of local shifters that they once spared, and that owe them big? Could be fun.<br /> Pack fetish: A sacred fetish part of the pack that is bound to each member of the pack. This is the pack ancestral connection or bond to their legacy (or something else Im just tossing stuff here). This could be an ancient fetish from the packs first hunt or taken from the largest spiritual prey they took donw. Maybe it is a small coin made the year the pack was formed. Powers could be stuff that connect the pack even closer. or a fetish that gives everyone in the pack protection from specific sources of damage, or you know the good ol' give extra damage with weaponry or brawl.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:12:30-07:00","id":860968,"title":"","content":"Forgot one thing. Pack merits related to protectorates or Confederacies (of you are playing with the Anshega). Ties that bind packs together.<br /> Oh and a way for players to build not only their pack but to help ST build in other packs in the area/ country/ State.<br /> last part is a bit on the side of the merit thing. But it would be cool to let players be a part of this world building.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}